# The Dockerfile compiles nothing — it COPYs one prebuilt binary out of dist/server (see
# scripts/build-artifacts.sh). So the build context is exactly that directory and nothing else.
#
# Excluding everything by default is the security property that matters here: no .env, no *.pem, no
# .git, no source tree can be swept into a layer that lives on in the build host's cache and in
# `docker history`. Adding a COPY to this Dockerfile means adding its source to the allow-list
# below, deliberately.
*
!dist/server
